🚀 TOP 10 SPRING BOOT DEPLOYMENT CONFIGURATIONS FOR KUBERNETES & AWS ECS
Senior Java Developer Interview Revision Sheet

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
☸️ KUBERNETES DEPLOYMENT CONFIGURATIONS
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

1. DEPLOYMENT

Purpose:
    Deploy and manage Spring Boot Pods.

YAML:

    apiVersion: apps/v1
    kind: Deployment

    metadata:
      name: springboot-app

    spec:
      replicas: 2

✅ Features:

    • Creates Pods
    • Self Healing
    • Rolling Updates
    • Scaling

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

2. SERVICE

Purpose:
    Expose Spring Boot application inside/outside cluster.

YAML:

    apiVersion: v1
    kind: Service

    spec:
      selector:
        app: springboot-app

      ports:
        - port: 80
          targetPort: 8080

Flow:

    Client
      ↓
    Service
      ↓
    Pods

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

3. CONFIGMAP

Purpose:
    Store environment-specific configuration.

YAML:

    envFrom:
      - configMapRef:
          name: app-config

Examples:

    • Database URL
    • API URLs
    • Feature Flags

❌ Not for passwords

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

4. SECRET

Purpose:
    Store sensitive configuration.

YAML:

    env:
      - name: DB_PASSWORD
        valueFrom:
          secretKeyRef:
            name: db-secret
            key: password

Examples:

    • Passwords
    • API Keys
    • Certificates
    • JWT Secrets

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

5. RESOURCE REQUESTS & LIMITS

Purpose:
    Prevent resource starvation.

YAML:

    resources:

      requests:
        cpu: "200m"
        memory: "512Mi"

      limits:
        cpu: "500m"
        memory: "1Gi"

Interview Answer:

    Requests = Minimum guaranteed resources

    Limits = Maximum permitted resources

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

6. READINESS PROBE

Purpose:
    Checks whether application can serve traffic.

YAML:

    readinessProbe:
      httpGet:
        path: /actuator/health/readiness
        port: 8080

If Probe Fails:

    Pod remains running

    Traffic is stopped

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

7. LIVENESS PROBE

Purpose:
    Checks whether application is alive.

YAML:

    livenessProbe:
      httpGet:
        path: /actuator/health/liveness
        port: 8080

If Probe Fails:

    Pod restarted automatically

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

8. INGRESS

Purpose:
    Expose application through URL.

YAML:

    apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1
    kind: Ingress

    spec:
      rules:
        - host: api.bank.com

Flow:

    Internet
       ↓
    Ingress
       ↓
    Service
       ↓
    Pods

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

9. HORIZONTAL POD AUTOSCALER (HPA)

Purpose:
    Auto-scale Pods.

YAML:

    apiVersion: autoscaling/v2
    kind: HorizontalPodAutoscaler

    spec:
      minReplicas: 2
      maxReplicas: 10

Example:

    CPU > 70%

    2 Pods
       ↓
    10 Pods

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

10. PERSISTENT VOLUME CLAIM (PVC)

Purpose:
    Persistent Storage.

YAML:

    volumes:
      - name: app-storage

        persistentVolumeClaim:
          claimName: app-pvc

Used For:

    • Logs
    • Files
    • Uploads

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
🏆 MOST ASKED FULL KUBERNETES DEPLOYMENT YAML
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

    apiVersion: apps/v1
    kind: Deployment

    metadata:
      name: springboot-app

    spec:
      replicas: 2

      selector:
        matchLabels:
          app: springboot-app

      template:

        metadata:
          labels:
            app: springboot-app

        spec:

          containers:

            - name: springboot-app

              image: myrepo/springboot:1.0

              ports:
                - containerPort: 8080

              envFrom:
                - configMapRef:
                    name: app-config

              readinessProbe:
                httpGet:
                  path: /actuator/health/readiness
                  port: 8080

              livenessProbe:
                httpGet:
                  path: /actuator/health/liveness
                  port: 8080

              resources:

                requests:
                  cpu: "200m"
                  memory: "512Mi"

                limits:
                  cpu: "500m"
                  memory: "1Gi"

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
☁️ AWS ECS DEPLOYMENT CONFIGURATIONS
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

1. ECS CLUSTER

Purpose:
    Logical group of ECS Services.

Structure:

    ECS Cluster
    ├── Payment Service
    ├── Customer Service
    └── Notification Service

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

2. ECS SERVICE

Purpose:
    Maintains desired number of Tasks.

Example:

    Desired Count = 2

    If one Task crashes:
        ↓
    Automatically recreated

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

3. ECS TASK DEFINITION

Purpose:
    Blueprint of container.

Contains:

    • Docker Image
    • CPU
    • Memory
    • Ports
    • Environment Variables
    • IAM Roles

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

4. ECS EXECUTION ROLE

Used By:
    ECS Runtime

Allows:

    • Pull Images from ECR
    • Send Logs to CloudWatch

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

5. ECS TASK ROLE

Used By:
    Application

Allows Access To:

    • S3
    • SNS
    • SQS
    • Secrets Manager
    • Parameter Store

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

6. AMAZON ECR

Purpose:
    Docker Image Repository.

Commands:

    docker build -t springboot-app .

    docker push <ecr-url>

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

7. APPLICATION LOAD BALANCER (ALB)

Purpose:
    Routes traffic to healthy tasks.

Flow:

    User
      ↓
    ALB
      ↓
    ECS Tasks

Supports:

    • SSL
    • Path Routing
    • Health Checks

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

8. CLOUDWATCH LOGS

Purpose:
    Centralized Logging.

Flow:

    Spring Boot Logs
            ↓
      CloudWatch

Sample Configuration:

    {
      "logConfiguration": {
        "logDriver": "awslogs"
      }
    }

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

9. SECRETS MANAGER

Purpose:
    Store sensitive credentials.

Stores:

    • Database Passwords
    • API Tokens
    • Certificates

Never Store In:

    • application.yml
    • Dockerfile
    • GitHub

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

10. ECS AUTO SCALING

Purpose:
    Auto-scale Tasks.

Example:

    CPU > 70%

    2 Tasks
       ↓
    10 Tasks

Configured Using:

    • CloudWatch Alarms
    • Target Tracking

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
🏆 MOST ASKED ECS TASK DEFINITION
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

    {
      "family": "springboot-task",

      "networkMode": "awsvpc",

      "requiresCompatibilities": [
        "FARGATE"
      ],

      "cpu": "512",

      "memory": "1024",

      "containerDefinitions": [
        {
          "name": "springboot-app",

          "image": "ecr-url/springboot:latest",

          "portMappings": [
            {
              "containerPort": 8080
            }
          ],

          "environment": [
            {
              "name": "SPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE",
              "value": "prod"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }

